<p>King Charles III addressed a joint session of the U.S. Congress in Washington on Tuesday, calling for reconciliation, renewal and continued cooperation between the United Kingdom and the United States during a rare speech by a British monarch. Charles and Queen Camilla were on a four-day state visit. He marked the 250th anniversary of American independence from Britain and told lawmakers the two countries had built “one of the most consequential alliances in human history”. The speech followed a White House welcome by President Trump and meetings with Republican and Democratic leaders on Capitol Hill. Charles did not directly mention the Iran war in his congressional address, but several accounts said U.S.-U.K. ties have been strained by President Trump’s criticism of British Prime Minister Keir Starmer over Britain’s level of support for U.S.-led military action against Iran. Charles urged the allies not to become “ever more inward-looking,” called for NATO unity, and said “unyielding resolve” was needed to secure a just and lasting peace in Ukraine. At the White House, Trump greeted Charles and Queen Camilla during a South Lawn ceremony and later hosted the royal couple for a state dinner.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ghM4ll5jznjPWa2sMlMI5AFQdZ_I5WCvWmdrboYOsjsEwYoq1ScezhVQAj0hZVzcfp-_7Hy8-uyaAOwdu_KXyKzfzV9BPVjrbKTXP4t55vrcHm8CV0abatAJHFREOQHtQpbW1Vxcjz86iyYigy0iavQi7vSqjkjzVjiu5YyxPODi1RJVwXqboMHznEmTt17GgjZRGx8bPfVGm0fCN2poBh515_ymCd-epwOUnSuyR4VJetiIL19e7MgQww' alt='Britain&#x27;s King Charles addresses a joint meeting of Congress, next to U.S. Vice President JD Vance and U.S. House Speaker Mike Johnson, in the House Chamber of the U.S. Capitol in Washington, DC, April 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Congressional reception: Charles entered the chamber with Queen Camilla and received a prolonged standing ovation before his remarks.</li><li>AUKUS detail: Royal aides also cited the trilateral AUKUS pact with Australia as one of the shared security interests tied to the address.</li><li>Democratic values: Charles referred to Congress as a “citadel of democracy” and discussed the rule of law, including Magna Carta and the U.S. Bill of Rights.</li><li>Next stops: The royal couple’s itinerary after Washington included Virginia and New York City.</li></ul><blockquote>Whatever our differences, whatever disagreements we may have, we stand united in our commitment to uphold democracy, to protect all our people from harm, and to salute the courage of those who daily risk their lives in the service of our countries, - King Charles III</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>King Charles III: Charles condemned political violence, telling lawmakers that “such acts of violence will never succeed” after authorities described a shooting at the White House Correspondents’ Dinner as an attempted assassination against Trump. (<a href='https://www.kron4.com/news/king-charles-iii-will-meet-trump-address-congress-in-a-bid-to-spotlight-uk-us-ties/'>KRON4</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump joked during the rainy White House welcome that it was a “beautiful British day.” (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/live-updates-king-charles-and-queen-camilla-visit-washington'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>British royal aides: Aides said trade, technology and security disputes were also part of the backdrop to the visit, along with the argument over Iran. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2026/04/27/congress/what-king-charles-will-tell-congress-00894459'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Tehran: Iran denied seeking nuclear weapons, maintaining that its nuclear program is for civilian purposes under international agreements. (<a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/uk-us-unity-tested-as-two-kings-meet-amid-iran-tensions/'>Hum English</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/28/nx-s1-5802803/king-charles-urges-reconciliation-in-address-to-u-s-congress-amid-trump-tensions'>King Charles ur